{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to the resident-memory figures cited in this request. The evidence page now records a range, not a slope: harness peak RSS is 83 MB at depth 100, 92 MB at 257 and 90 MB at 500, which is not monotonic, and the depth-1000 reading is on the checkpoint path. Depths 100-500 give 17.5 KB per record; the live resident's 347 MiB at 5,786 records over an 80 MB base gives 47 KB. PREVIEW therefore lands between 875 MB and 2.4 GB against a 1 GiB target and is UNDECIDED, not the miss this request's conditions assert. FIRST-PRODUCTION misses across the whole range, needing at least 8.75 GB against 4 GiB, so the request itself stands. Its conditions of satisfaction are unchanged: establish the slope by measurement and keep 50,000 records under 1 GiB."}